<Placemark>   <name>Das Quellenreuther Steinkreuz</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Bavaria <b>Alt Name:</b> Quellenreuth I <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 50.23763 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 11.9832389<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Germany/Bavaria/thumb/krt_P3101362.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Up to 82 cm tall granite standing stone just by the junction near the village of Quellenreuth. The stone is most probably a medieval cross stone. Today it is severely weathered and its true shape can ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=51936" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>11.9832389,50.23763,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Dörenther Steinkreuze</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> North Rhine-Westphalia <b>Alt Name:</b> Dörenther Sühnekreuze <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>2</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 52.237899 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 7.693739<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Germany/NorthRhineWestphalia/thumb/Cresta_2016_Okt_SuehnekreuzeDoerenthe_2aRS.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Two historic monolithic sandstone crosses. Possibly they are late medieval conciliation crosses, though their exact age is unknown.. The smaller one (Dörenthe I) faces West and measures 150 x 75 x 30...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=46191" >Link To More Information</a><br />
